insert into blog_posts (slug, title, excerpt, content, author, published, published_at) values ('acrylic-vs-polycarbonate', 'Acrylic vs Polycarbonate: Which Material Fits Your Application?', 'Both are common choices for transparent fabricated components, but they suit different jobs. Here''s how to think about the choice.', 'Acrylic and polycarbonate are the two materials we fabricate with, and they''re often considered for the same kind of component — a guard, a window, an enclosure — which makes the choice between them a genuinely common question.
insert into blog_posts (slug, title, excerpt, content, author, published, published_at) values ('choosing-acrylic-thickness', 'Choosing Acrylic Thickness: What Actually Matters', 'There''s no single right thickness — it depends on span, load, and how the part is mounted. Here''s what to think through before you specify one.', 'We get asked about acrylic thickness more than almost anything else, and the honest answer is that there isn''t a default — the right thickness depends on the part, not a rule of thumb.
insert into blog_posts (slug, title, excerpt, content, author, published, published_at) values ('industrial-machine-guards', 'What Makes a Good Industrial Machine Guard', 'A machine guard has one job that matters more than any other: staying between a person and a hazard. Here''s what that means for material and fabrication choices.', 'A machine guard exists to do one thing: keep a person separated from a hazard while the process behind it keeps running. Everything about how it''s specified and built follows from that.
insert into blog_posts (slug, title, excerpt, content, author, published, published_at) values ('acrylic-fabrication', 'What Acrylic Fabrication Actually Involves', 'From flat sheet to a finished component — an overview of the processes that turn acrylic stock into a usable part.', '"Acrylic fabrication" covers a handful of distinct processes, and most real components need more than one of them combined.
insert into blog_posts (slug, title, excerpt, content, author, published, published_at) values ('polycarbonate-fabrication', 'Polycarbonate Fabrication: What''s Different From Acrylic', 'The same core processes apply, but polycarbonate''s properties change a few things about how it''s handled and where it''s used.', 'Polycarbonate goes through largely the same fabrication processes as acrylic — cutting, CNC routing, bending, bonding — but its properties change how each of those gets approached and what it''s typically used for.
insert into blog_posts (slug, title, excerpt, content, author, published, published_at) values ('cnc-acrylic-cutting', 'CNC Acrylic Cutting: When Routing Is the Right Call', 'CNC routing and laser cutting can both produce a cut acrylic part — here''s how to think about which one fits your geometry.', 'CNC routing is computer-controlled cutting guided directly by a drawing or CAD file, and it''s one of the two main ways we cut acrylic — the other being laser cutting.
insert into blog_posts (slug, title, excerpt, content, author, published, published_at) values ('laser-cutting', 'Laser Cutting Acrylic and Polycarbonate: Where It Excels', 'Laser cutting isn''t a replacement for CNC routing — it''s the better tool for a specific kind of geometry.', 'Laser cutting uses a guided laser rather than a mechanical bit to cut through sheet material, and the difference in method is exactly why it suits different work than CNC routing does.
insert into blog_posts (slug, title, excerpt, content, author, published, published_at) values ('acrylic-bending', 'Acrylic Bending: Getting a Folded Edge Without a Seam', 'Heat-forming acrylic to an angle avoids a bonded corner entirely — useful more often than it gets considered.', 'Acrylic bending heat-forms a sheet to a specified angle, producing a folded or curved component from a single piece rather than two pieces joined at a bonded corner.
insert into blog_posts (slug, title, excerpt, content, author, published, published_at) values ('acrylic-bonding', 'Acrylic Bonding: How Multi-Part Assemblies Get Built', 'Bonding is how a component too large or too complex for a single sheet becomes one finished assembly.', 'Bonding joins separate acrylic (or polycarbonate) pieces into a single finished assembly, using solvent or adhesive bonding depending on the joint and the application.
insert into blog_posts (slug, title, excerpt, content, author, published, published_at) values ('industrial-applications', 'Where Acrylic and Polycarbonate Fabrication Actually Gets Used', 'A tour through the industrial applications where fabricated acrylic and polycarbonate components show up — and why.', 'Fabricated acrylic and polycarbonate components show up across a wider range of industrial applications than people usually expect, and the common thread across almost all of them is the same: something needs to be seen through while also being protected, contained, or guarded.
